# ── Derived audio (regenerable from the ROM; 350 MB of copyrighted audio) ─────
# The tracked sound decomp is audio/dtpk/*.json — the DTPK manifests, which
# carry only ROM-derived fields and are proven byte-exact by
# `make dtpk-roundtrip`.  Everything below is OUTPUT, not decomp data:
#   audio/raw/       byte-exact payloads, regenerated by `make dtpk-unpack`
#   audio/samples/   ADPCM decoded to PCM16 WAV — lossy, cannot rebuild the ROM
#   audio/sequences/ MIDI from the RETRACTED converter (see below) — fabricated
#   audio/banks/, audio/sample_table.json, audio/song_to_bank.json
#                    superseded by audio/dtpk/, and they assert a constant
#                    "pitch": "C5" on every sample, which is not a ROM fact
audio/raw/
audio/samples/
# textures/raw/
# data/rom/ likewise: regenerable by `make rom-unpack`.
data/rom/ is the same idea: regenerable by `make texture-unpack`; the
# tracked graphics decomp is textures/stx/*.json.
textures/raw/
# data/rom/ likewise: regenerable by `make rom-unpack`.
data/rom/
audio/sequences/
audio/banks/
audio/sample_table.json
audio/song_to_bank.json

